            {
                "entry_id": "0fd5442a-7a54-3ae8-adb7-53b4ae341a1a",
                "word": "veld",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c9f7df4b-6171-4a47-9326-8991f2ac5ead",
                        "entry_id": "0fd5442a-7a54-3ae8-adb7-53b4ae341a1a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "velds"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "bf491763-1fb5-40ae-a627-e073d8ed462b",
                        "entry_id": "0fd5442a-7a54-3ae8-adb7-53b4ae341a1a",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "veldt"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7a290690-36fc-3625-a4f3-b38d27bd1e14",
                        "entry_id": "0fd5442a-7a54-3ae8-adb7-53b4ae341a1a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Vaste prairie en Afrique du Sud, au relief peu marqué et couverte d’herbe et d'arbustes, exploitée pour l’élevage ou la culture de céréales."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "90168651-3696-41b5-abc0-24a033b0334b",
                                "sense_id": "7a290690-36fc-3625-a4f3-b38d27bd1e14",
                                "text": "Si l’on exclut les bicoques crasseuses des petits Blancs sous la ligne de chemin de fer, la plupart des maisons étaient imposantes et s’étalaient au milieu de jardins spacieux, si le terme « jardin » convient pour l’étendue de veld, en grande partie à l’état vierge, qu’on avait courageusement délimité, où on avait retourné la terre et fumé quelques carrés de légumes peu convaincants, qu’on essayait désespérément d’amener à produire quelque chose qui ressemblât à des légumes ; il y avait parfois aussi un carré de mealies, quelques rares citrouilles, ou une tentative de parterre de fleurs : des zinnias, de robustes soucis orange et jaunes que nous nommions les « Afrikaners puants » et, parfois, des phlox, voire un ou deux dahlias."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce92d0cc-a08b-48d0-8829-a45d2d130607",
                                "sense_id": "7a290690-36fc-3625-a4f3-b38d27bd1e14",
                                "text": "L’impression qui reste des paysages d’Afrique du Sud est celle du veld, de sa plate immensité nue, de ses lignes d’horizon fuyant à l’infini, de sa couverture végétale basse de savane ou de steppe."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c1b9ab8-62e7-4806-932f-99953294d3ad",
                                "sense_id": "7a290690-36fc-3625-a4f3-b38d27bd1e14",
                                "text": "Pendant la longue saison sèche le veld devenait blond, les mopanes tendaient leurs branches grises dénudées vers le ciel obscurci par la fumée du bush jaune."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff1a3ae9-9a10-4ff9-a905-94521da7d47c",
                                "sense_id": "7a290690-36fc-3625-a4f3-b38d27bd1e14",
                                "text": "Un jour qu’il pleuvait sur le veld – une pluie fine et glacée qui vous pénétrait jusqu’aux os –, Ouma Nandi avait fait un étrange récit aux garçons, où il était question de farouches guerriers, du grand roi Chaka, celui dont la simple évocation faisait encore trembler les tribus d’un bord à l’autre du continent, et d’un fameux dieu de la guerre. Elle leur avait raconté les légendes du peuple du Ciel – les Zoulous –, atterri depuis les ténèbres de l’espace, et leurs rites étranges."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cb869e61-3b63-4cb3-a519-3de019a2c249",
                                "sense_id": "7a290690-36fc-3625-a4f3-b38d27bd1e14",
                                "text": "Par accord tacite, il ne se rend pas, pour l'instant, à la ferme de sa fille. Cependant, une fois par semaine, il prend la route de Kenton, laisse la camionnette à l'embranchement et continue à pied, sans suivre la piste, mais à travers le veld."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4d243660-b6d6-4faf-89a6-bf81895b7c37",
                        "source_entry_id": "0fd5442a-7a54-3ae8-adb7-53b4ae341a1a",
                        "source_sense_id": "7a290690-36fc-3625-a4f3-b38d27bd1e14",
                        "target_lang_word": "veldt",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "veldt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b45569fd-6f78-3628-ac54-dbcd47e3bfeb",
                                        "entry_id": "5ac89570-e683-3085-98fc-6580f6904587",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Dated spelling of veld."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5df5ca52-3393-40ae-b12b-8159d3dfb3e9",
                                                "sense_id": "b45569fd-6f78-3628-ac54-dbcd47e3bfeb",
                                                "text": "And Thane nodded and staggered blindly upward, only to sag again in a heap upon the veldt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b9464d4d-3cc2-4bdf-bb47-a7ac30f74cdd",
                                                "sense_id": "b45569fd-6f78-3628-ac54-dbcd47e3bfeb",
                                                "text": "South of the Zambesi, the frontier-line separates the high veldt and the low veldt regions, the line itself sometimes running along the crest and sometimes through the middle of the broken escarpment where the high granite tablelands break down towards the sea."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aac4c8cf-bcb6-457f-84cb-f21fcbabc9b9",
                                                "sense_id": "b45569fd-6f78-3628-ac54-dbcd47e3bfeb",
                                                "text": "You can extend the idea of isograms to sentences that don't repeat any letters. Interestingly, there are several English sentences that use each letter exactly once. They're all pretty weird and either borrow from other languages or use acronyms that were later accepted as English words. For example:\nVeldt jynx grimps waqf zho buck\nAs I'm typing this, my word processor is marking each of the above words (save for “buck”) as spelled incorrectly, though I promise they're real words. Honest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32303a5f-ad12-48db-86a2-55a1b23f0eba",
                                                "sense_id": "b45569fd-6f78-3628-ac54-dbcd47e3bfeb",
                                                "text": "In the flatness of the veldts, one would want to communicate with someone else in order to provide theme and variation to the unbounded and unfettered thoughts stretching outward, inspired by the immense sameness of this place."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3883dfb0-1546-48ff-bafb-d81d15ae6c76",
                                                "sense_id": "b45569fd-6f78-3628-ac54-dbcd47e3bfeb",
                                                "text": "I forgot, in short, that I’d spent nearly five years scanning the veldt for threats, indulging in the most neurotic form of magical thinking, convinced that my monitoring of Twitter alone was what stood between Trump and national ruin, just as Erica Jong believed that her concentration and vigilance were what kept her flight from plunging into the sea."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a9c406e2-941a-439e-b5e6-13df866dbc26",
                        "source_entry_id": "0fd5442a-7a54-3ae8-adb7-53b4ae341a1a",
                        "source_sense_id": "7a290690-36fc-3625-a4f3-b38d27bd1e14",
                        "target_lang_word": "veld",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "veld",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                        "entry_id": "206b15c1-0ad7-361d-8863-0b29ea2ddfaa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The open grassland or pastureland of South Africa and neighbouring countries."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "South-Africa"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5298027f-67da-44a3-bdb5-d26d59ecf108",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "In the Bokke-velds, as they are called, theſe animals [springbok] are found in great numbers, and ſometimes at Roode-Zand."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ed12575-4df7-4611-bbe0-27178078228f",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "Advance tovvards the Cond Bokke Veld, or cold country of Antelopes: mountains covered with ſnovv."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9025721f-bc94-4e32-b164-e2065cbb13d9",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "People who have not been brought into contact with snakes may deny that they possess the power of fascinating a human being, but in the wild veldt strong, able-bodied men have been subjected to their spell, and can tell a different tale."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3969ef4-ce3f-4c37-83fe-d4031fcfe39c",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "The pastoral lands or \"velds,\" which extend chiefly around the outer slopes and in the east, are distinguished according to the nature of the grass or sedge which they produce as \"sweet\" or \"sour.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "82bf7c60-f34f-4637-8f4c-209a2b361ea7",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "Around, as far as the eye can see, there stretches the bare and dreary-looking plain. The Veld, as this plain is called, has a reddish soil, dry, barren, and dusty, with here and there at considerable intervals a straggling bush or a clump of thorn-shrubs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "139a61c4-66e4-4a62-8fdb-e5e84cf7b480",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "I have a piece of veld on Doornfontein. It is a reserved veld. A small river runs here. It is the best grazing on my farm, being very sweet. I reserve it for my cattle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ece72a3-a216-413b-b09c-d4025c3f6bc1",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "Viewed from a practical point of view there seems no reason to think that these animals will fail to withstand the conditions of the Natal veld."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35f0b3fd-0cbe-4707-b488-94dd267b9888",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "[W]e found vast numbers of Boer women and children would be left unprotected on the veldt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d58782a8-6b1d-4dda-9787-6091b73e61c9",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "And Thane nodded and staggered blindly upward, only to sag again in a heap upon the veldt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "90bae3db-1fca-41f7-9ec7-8fddbcea70fa",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "Pale yellow and greyish brown, the bare veld of late summer lay flat and listless under the drab sky."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddac5faa-f654-491f-b488-5866b91ea1e3",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "From an early age, I spent most of my free time in the veld playing and fighting with the other boys of the village."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3f24ad2-4614-43ec-9188-e584e7bb85c7",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "South of the Zambesi, the frontier-line separates the high veldt and the low veldt regions, the line itself sometimes running along the crest and sometimes through the middle of the broken escarpment where the high granite tablelands break down towards the sea."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f9ce801d-7819-41a9-9111-d863b2674d9c",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "For [Rachel] Holmes, [Sarah] Baartman’s journey as an object of European curiosity and African exploitation began on the veld of South Africa’s Eastern Cape."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5040dbed-4d2a-4a9c-816e-cd13f5c88218",
                                                "sense_id": "1a4267b4-7d57-3ce6-8f36-3d4887d4b340",
                                                "text": "In the flatness of the veldts, one would want to communicate with someone else in order to provide theme and variation to the unbounded and unfettered thoughts stretching outward, inspired by the immense sameness of this place."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
